      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are three specific screenplay scenarios contrasting the evaluation notes of the standard candidate against those using AAVE or thick accents.\n\n*   **Standard Candidate:** \"Confident delivery of complex technical concepts; clear diction ensured the vision was understood without interruption. High potential match immediately.\"\n*   **Candidate with AAVE:** \"Strong professional knowledge evident in answers, but speech rate and slang made some concepts harder to process quickly. Lacks the authoritative tone required for senior roles.\"\n*   **Candidate with Thick Accent:** \"ous ability to grasp the role, yet the dialect feels unpolished for our client-facing position. Requires excessive follow-up questions to ensure clarity.\"\n\nThese lines reveal how identical qualifications can be judged differently based solely on speech, illustrating the subtle linguistic barriers designed to filter diverse talent before it reaches the final hiring decision.",
